#more and less and tab completion

#more is a command that views text files or long command outputs one screen at a time. 
#more mainly moves forward. Less is also a text viewing command tool. Less moves in both directions.
# more loads the whole file before viewing, while less only loads what fits on your screen , which
#makes it beteer for huge log files.
#more exits automatically once the end of the file is reached, while less always stays pen until
# you press q to close.

less filename.txt
more filename.txt

#work with pipe operator

ls -la | less
dmesg | more

# in less -
#spacebar or page down go to next page
# b or page up go to previous page
# down arrow or enter go down one line
# up arrow or k go up one line
# /word searches for text
# q quits
# N previous intance of word and n next instance of word
# g top of file and G EOF

#in more -
# spacebar next page
# b previous page (doesnt work with pipes, only files)
# enter down one line
#/word search text
#q or reach EOF to quit

